### Article 15

Coordinating group for protection from domestic violence

1.	The National Coordinator against violence leads the Inter-ministerial Coordinating Group against domestic violence, violence against women and gender-based violence with the following composition:
1.1.	Office of the Prime Minister - Agency for Gender Equality, deputy chairperson;  

1.2.	Ministry responsible for internal affairs, member;  

1.3.	Ministry responsible for finance, labor and transfers, member;  

1.4.	Ministry responsible for Justice, member;  

1.5.	Ministry responsible for health, member;  

1.6.	Ministry responsible for education, member;  

1.7.	Ministry responsible for local government, member; and

1.8.	Ministry responsible for culture, youth and sports, member;  

LAW NO. 08/L-185 ON THE PREVENTION AND PROTECTION FROM DOMESTIC VIOLENCE, VIOLENCE AGAINST WOMEN AND GENDER-BASED VIOLENCE

1.9.	Kosovo Police, member;  

1.10.	State Prosecution, member;  

1.11.	Kosovo Judicial Council, member;  

1.12.	Academy of Justice, member;  

1.13.	Coalition of Shelters of Kosovo, member;  

1.14.	Office for Victim Protection and Assistance, member, and

1.15.	Representative of the Center for Social Work, member.  

2.	Permanent members as representatives of ministries are the responsible deputy ministers. In case of inability, they may delegate membership to an official of the responsible cabinet.  

3.	At the invitation of the Chairperson / National Coordinator, representatives of other ministries and other relevant institutions may also be invited, depending on the obligations arising from the strategy for protection from domestic violence, as well as representatives of civil society organizations and strategic partners in the capacity of observers.  

4.	The Inter-ministerial Coordinating Group exercises the following duties and responsibilities:

4.1.	Implementation, review and overall evaluation of the Strategy for Protection from Domestic Violence and the Action Plan;  

4.2.	The National Coordinator and the Inter-ministerial Coordination Group serves as the coordinating body responsible for coordination, implementation, monitoring and evaluation of policies and measures for the prevention and combating of all forms of violence covered by this Law and the Council of Europe Convention on preventing and combating violence against women and domestic violence;  

4.3.	Coordination of all activities within the country with the aim of ensuring inter-institutional and inter-sectoral cooperation, including data collection and processing, ensuring budget, human resources for the implementation of the strategy.  

5.	All institutions at all levels are obliged to respond to all requests of the Coordinating Group for protection from domestic violence.

### Article 16

Responsibilities of Victim Advocates

1.	The duties and responsibilities of victim advocates under this Law include but are not limited to:

1.1.	Meeting the victim immediately after the referral of the domestic violence case to the police;  

1.2.	Informing the victim about his or her rights, the assistance that is available and the procedures for protection orders;  

1.3.	Preparing the request for a protection order with the consent of the victim and collecting the documentation/evidence necessary to support the request;  

1.4.	Submitting the request for a protection order to the court after obtaining consent from the victim or his or her legal representative;  

LAW NO. 08/L-185 ON THE PREVENTION AND PROTECTION FROM DOMESTIC VIOLENCE, VIOLENCE AGAINST WOMEN AND GENDER-BASED VIOLENCE

1.5.	Representing the victim in court in all hearings for the request for a protection order and assisting in the preparation of submissions and other legal instruments.  

2.	Any assistance and action related to the procedure for requesting protection orders is done based on the consent of the victim.  

3.	In addition to the obligations in representing the victim in the procedure for requesting protection orders, the victim advocate also informs the victim about his or her right to compensation from the state, guides and assists the victim in submitting the request for compensation in accordance with the Law on Compensation of Victims.

### Article 17

Duties and responsibilities of educational and scientific institutions

1.	The relevant Ministry for Education, in addition to the general preventive measures specified in Article 10. of this Law, in accordance with its scope of activity, also undertakes the following special preventive measures:

1.1.	Includes in the curriculum of pre-university levels of education, topics that promote gender equality, non-violent conflict resolution, respect for diversity, knowledge about gender identity, all forms of gender-based violence and comprehensive sexual education;  

1.2.	Organizes for educational staff continuous basic and professional training on gender equality, mutual respect, the right to personal integrity, non-violent conflict resolution, respect for diversity, and ensuring knowledge about all forms of gender-based violence and comprehensive sexual education.  

2.	Higher education institutions include in their curriculum issues that address gender equality, gender identity, respect for diversity, domestic violence, violence against women and gender-based violence.

### Article 18

Programs for the prevention of repetition of violence

1.	The relevant ministries for justice, education and health are obliged to create special psychosocial treatment programs, with the aim of changing violent behavior and special treatment programs for perpetrators of sexual violence.  

2.	The programs from paragraph 1 of this article have as their main objective the prevention of repetition of violence.

