### Article 21

Responsibilities of the Centre for Social Work

1.	The duties and responsibilities of the Centres for Social Work (CSW), according to this Law include:

1.1.	Intervening in every case when contacted by the Kosovo Police;  

1.2.	Intervening ex officio, in every case when domestic violence is suspected and intervening in cases when contacted by actors in the referral system for protection from domestic violence;  

1.3.	Every identified and referred victim is assigned a case manager, who is a professional within the CSW to lead the process of social protection of the victim in identifying, coordinating and providing all existing social services;  

1.4.	Contacting the adult and child victim immediately after identification and referral of the domestic violence case;  

1.5.	Appointment by the head of social services, of the legal guardian who represents the best interest of the child in cases when children are victims of domestic violence by biological parents or guardian;  

LAW NO. 08/L-185 ON PREVENTION AND PROTECTION FROM DOMESTIC VIOLENCE VIOLENCE AGAINST WOMEN AND GENDER-BASED VIOLENCE

1.6.	Taking urgent measures for the protection of the dignity, rights and interests of the child, by the CSW when it learns of the existing risk to the child due to abuse of parental rights or any risk to the child from serious neglect of parental duties;  

1.7.	When the Guardianship Authority has reasonable grounds to believe that there is a serious direct risk to the health, safety or well-being of the child, the guardianship authority may enter any place and remove the child to a safe place, where he/she will have care for a period not exceeding 72 hours;  

1.8.	The case manager, after assessing the situation within the framework of social protection and integration, supports and refers the survivor to rehabilitation and employment programs, for empowerment and independent living;  

1.9.	Before the expiry of the 72-hour period, the guardianship authority must present the case to the competent court, which decides on the guardianship of the child. If circumstances require, the court may issue an assessment order for a period of 21 days, to enable further investigations and assessments, by which time the case must be presented to court for further consideration. With the placement of the child under the protection of the Guardianship Authority, the other rights belonging to the parents do not cease, nor their duties towards the child;  

1.10.	In coordination with other institutions and based on the assessment of the victim's needs or the victim's personal risk, provides temporary shelter for victims of domestic violence;  

1.11.	The CSW based on the request from the competent justice authorities is obliged to prepare the social anamnesis for each case;  

1.12.	In every case of domestic violence it is obliged to refer or offer psychosocial counseling for the victim of domestic violence or against women and persons dependent on him/her;  

1.13.	The CSW in coordination with other institutions provides temporary shelter for victims of domestic violence and against women and persons dependent on him/her;  

1.14.	The case manager in the process of supporting the victim coordinates activities for reintegration;  

1.15.	The CSW is obliged to follow the victim's case until the closure of the case from the aspect of social protection;  

1.16.	At the request of the protected party or ex officio when the protected party is a child, compiles and submits the request for protection order and participates in court proceedings according to this Law;  

1.17.	The CSW must implement the court decision regarding the fulfillment of obligations arising from the decision and in case of non-fulfillment of obligations must inform the court through a report on the reasons for non-fulfillment;  

1.18.	The case manager after assessing the situation refers the case to the social assistance scheme service for all cases which have no income or have no obstacles based on legislation in force for social schemes.  

2.	Centres for social work must create an emergency fund for the needs of victims during the period when they are in police. Procedures for this matter are regulated by sub-legal act

