issued by the relevant Ministry for Justice.

### Article 22

Support services for victims

1.	For the purpose of preventing and alleviating the consequences of domestic violence and effective implementation of protective measures for the victim within the framework of this law, the institutions of the Republic of Kosovo depending on the field of administrative responsibility, offer support services as follows:

1.1.	Informing the victim about her rights and existing services in the community;  
1.2.	Temporary shelter of the victim of domestic violence and other persons, in cases when they must be removed from the living space, where there is a risk of repetition of violence;  

1.3.	Providing emergency health care, and other health services as needed;  

1.4.	Free legal aid and free legal representation in court during protection order request proceedings and other civil or criminal proceedings;  

1.5.	Referring the victim to the compensation program and assisting with the submission of the compensation request;  

1.6.	Providing psychosocial treatment and other rehabilitation programs, according to the victim's needs;  

1.7.	Providing counseling, orientation and vocational training programs or ensuring that victims of domestic violence participate in vocational training from regional vocational training centers and employment offices and third parties;  

1.8.	Providing employment opportunities programs and other reintegration programs;  

1.9.	Providing educational programs and opportunities to continue education for the victim and her children;  

1.10.	Providing financial support through existing social assistance services, if cases when conditions are met according to legislation in force;  

1.11.	Providing permanent shelter for victims of domestic violence through social housing or financial support for enabling shelter;  

1.12.	Support services are secured and offered also by licensed organizations in accordance with this Law;  

1.13.	Support services for victims are offered free of charge and without discrimination and are financed from the budget of the Republic of Kosovo;  

1.14.	All employees of victim support services will be required to undergo mandatory continuous training with gender sensitivity in accordance with guidelines and curriculum that focuses on prevention and detection of violence, equality between women and men, needs and rights of victims, such as prevention of secondary victimization and coordinated multi-agency cooperation to ensure complete and proper handling of referrals.  

